WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.925
The headline finding is a large, previously
unquantified gap.

00:00:04.005 --> 00:00:09.243
Adversarially trained classifiers perform far worse
than the theoretical optimum,

00:00:09.323 --> 00:00:14.692
and this gap is much wider than what prior work
observed for binary classification.

00:00:14.772 --> 00:00:16.005
On 3-class CIFAR-10,

00:00:16.085 --> 00:00:21.783
TRADES adversarial training cannot achieve a loss
much better than 0.6 at a perturbation

00:00:21.863 --> 00:00:25.919
strength where the optimal achievable loss is
essentially zero.

00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:27.494
In the 10-class setting,

00:00:27.574 --> 00:00:34.322
the efficient lower and upper bounds sandwich the
optimal loss tightly for the budgets used in practice,

00:00:34.402 --> 00:00:37.342
so the gap is not an artifact of loose bounds.

00:00:37.422 --> 00:00:43.120
This suggests current robust training struggles far
more as the number of classes grows.
